 the manufacturing industry.", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/idahomanufacturingalliance/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='idaho-manufacturing-alliance' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ideal Fabricators Inc. operates from Livonia, Michigan, where it was founded in 1984 by Patrick Purdom to serve the machine tool industry across the state. The company expanded its plant and crane capacity in 1998 to handle larger fabrications and reach customers beyond Michigan. In 2003 it partnered with Statewide Boring & Machine to offer complete fabricated and machined parts throughout North America, and Statewide Boring more than doubled its plant footprint in 2011 to accommodate new CNC equipment. In 2022 the business transitioned to 100 percent employee ownership.

The shop provides heavy steel plate fabrication, large CNC machining, precision plate burning, and heat-treat and straightening services. Its expanded facilities allow end-to-end production so that a single purchase order can cover fabrication, machining, laser inspection, and finish painting.

While the original customer base was the Michigan machine tool sector, the company now ships to manufacturers across the United States and Canada.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Heavy steel plate fabrication", "Large CNC machining", "Precision plate burning", "Heat treating", "Straightening", "Laser inspection", "Finish painting"], "industries": ["Machine tool", "Heavy machinery", "Energy", "Transportation", "Industrial equipment"], "materials": ["Steel plate"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single purchase order covers fabrication, machining, laser inspection, and finish painting", "Plant expansions in 1998 and 2011 increased capacity for large fabrications", "100% employee-owned since 2022", "Serves customers across the United States and Canada"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1984 by Patrick Purdom -> /about", "1998 plant size and crane capacity doubled -> /about", "2003 partnered with Statewide Boring & Machine -> /about", "2011 Statewide Boring more than doubled plant size to add new CNC equipment -> /about", "2022 became 100% employee-owned -> /about", "Heavy steel plate fabricating, large CNC machining, precision plate burning -> /", "Heat treat & straightening solutions -> /", "One purchase order for fabricated, machined, laser inspected, finish painted parts -> /", "Serves all of North America -> /", "Located in Livonia, Michigan -> db", "Machine tool industry -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We provide heavy steel plate fabricating, large CNC machining, and precision plate burning.", "founded_year": "1984", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ideal-fabricators-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Illinois Culinary Equipment (ICE) is based in Chicago, Illinois. The company was founded by Michael Palombo, a classically trained chef who spent 25 years in professional kitchens, including roles as executive chef at the Carolina Inn in Chapel Hill, the University Park Hotel at MIT, and the Mount Washington Hotel in New Hampshire. After a stint as a sales manager for RATIONAL Cooking Systems, Palombo launched ICE as a manufacturers'' representative, initially partnering with Electrolux Professional before expanding to represent a full suite of commercial kitchen brands.

ICE does not manufacture equipment; instead, it provides commercial kitchen design, equipment specification, and project consulting for foodservice operators. The firm''s staff assists with concept development, space planning, traffic patterns, maintenance considerations, and budget management.

The company serves restaurants, hotels, institutional cafeterias, and specialty foodservice concepts such as carry-out delis and cook-and-chill kitchens. Its client base includes independent operators and multi-unit chains seeking expertise in kitchen layout and equipment selection.

