UPDATE companies SET description='Illinois Supply Company operates from Mokena, Illinois, and was founded with the creation of the Original Allergy Emergency Kit, a product now deployed in thousands of schools worldwide. The company is owned by Brandon Wilson, who also designed the original Overdose Emergency Kit that established the Naloxone Box category in 2014.

The company manufactures a range of emergency medical and harm reduction equipment, including naloxone cabinets, boxes, vending machines (such as the Barney freestanding kiosk), overdose emergency cabinets, and police pouches. It also produces epinephrine storage cabinets, Allergy Emergency Kits (AEK), school nurse storage panels, LiveSafer safety stations, AED cabinets, and bleeding control, asthma, and choking response kits. In 2024, the firm tripled its manufacturing and warehouse space to meet growing demand, and it emphasizes made-to-order production with ship-on-demand fulfillment for grant-funded programs.

Illinois Supply Company serves non-profit agencies, community health departments, school districts, correctional facilities, law enforcement, and state and county public health departments. Concrete clients include the Florida Department of Children and Family Services (203 drop-off locations, 1,880 kiosks and cabinets), Monroe County, New York (550 naloxone boxes), the California prison system, and numerous county health departments across New York, Pennsylvania, Kentucky, Illinois, and other states.

The business originated to address allergy emergencies in schools and later expanded into overdose harm reduction. Wilson states that the company invests heavily in capacity, develops new products monthly based on customer requests, and offers custom product design. It operates a website dedicated to non-profit agencies that does not charge sales tax and maintains government registrations (CAGE/UEI) for public procurement.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Naloxone cabinet manufacturing", "Naloxone vending machine manufacturing (Barney kiosk)", "Harm reduction supply vending machine manufacturing", "Overdose emergency cabinet manufacturing", "Naloxone police pouch manufacturing", "Outdoor naloxone cabinet manufacturing", "Customizable naloxone cabinet design", "Naloxone program website development", "Epinephrine storage cabinet manufacturing", "Allergy Emergency Kit (AEK) manufacturing", "School nurse epinephrine storage cabinet/panel manufacturing", "LiveSafer safety station manufacturing", "AED cabinet manufacturing", "Bleeding control kit manufacturing", "Asthma emergency kit manufacturing", "Choking safety station manufacturing", "Custom product design", "Label printing for AEK and LiveSafer products", "Photo label system integration", "AEK School Protection System deployment", "Product compatibility assessment", "Grant spending compliance and ship-on-demand fulfillment", "Government procurement (CAGE/UEI registration)"], "industries": ["Schools (K-12)", "Correctional facilities", "Community health departments", "Non-profit agencies", "Government agencies (state, county)", "Law enforcement", "Behavioral health organizations", "Public health departments", "Harm reduction organizations", "Food service"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Original Allergy Emergency Kit deployed in thousands of schools worldwide", "Designed the original Overdose Emergency Kit that created the Naloxone Box category in 2014", "Tripled manufacturing and warehouse space in 2024", "Custom product development driven by customer requests", "Ship-on-demand fulfillment for grant-funded programs"], "facts_used": ["Founded with Original Allergy Emergency Kit now in thousands of schools worldwide -> db", "Owner Brandon Wilson designed original Overdose Emergency Kit creating Naloxone Box category in 2014 -> /", "Manufactures naloxone cabinets, boxes, vending machines, overdose emergency cabinets, police pouches -> /", "Manufactures epinephrine storage cabinets, AEK, school nurse storage panels, LiveSafer safety stations, AED cabinets -> /", "Tripled manufacturing and warehouse space in 2024 -> /", "Made-to-order production with ship-on-demand for grant-funded programs -> /", "Serves non-profits, community health departments, schools, correctional facilities, law enforcement, public health departments -> /", "Florida Dept of Children and Family Services: 203 drop-off locations, 1,880 kiosks and cabinets -> db", "Monroe County NY: 550 naloxone boxes -> /", "California prison system client -> /", "Numerous county health departments across multiple states -> /", "Website for non-profit agencies, no sales tax -> /", "Government registrations (CAGE/UEI) -> /", "HQ: Mokena, Illinois -> db", "Custom product design and development based on customer requests -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "we have tripled our manufacturing and warehouse space", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='illinois-supply-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Illinois Switchboard Corporation was established in 1971 in Addison, Illinois. The company has operated continuously since its founding, focusing on electrical metering and distribution equipment.

The company manufactures and designs electrical switchboards (up to 4000 amp), power and lighting panelboards, industrial control panels, and electrical enclosures with welded steel construction. It also produces special sheetmetal fabrications and specializes in alterations and additions to existing switchboards, including bus details and circuit breaker retrofits for any brand. A quick-ship program offers NEMA 1 distribution panels in 60-, 75-, and 90-inch heights, with main lug ratings from 400 to 1200 amps and main breaker ratings from 400 to 800 amps. The firm stocks a large selection of Siemens circuit breakers, fusible switches, and components, and says it can handle orders ranging from one to 1,000 pieces.

Its engineering staff assists with design and retrofit questions.

